<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaston, Duke of Orléans</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1608">1608</a>–<a href="/years/1660">1660</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Gaston of Orléans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaston, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, was the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiii-of-france">Louis XIII of France</a> and for many years heir to the throne. He took part in repeated plots against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu">Cardinal Richelieu</a>, and in 1632 secretly married Marguerite of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, sister of Duke Charles IV, which helped provoke the French invasion of Lorraine. He later sided with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-fronde">Fronde</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jules-mazarin">Cardinal Mazarin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaston-duke-of-orleans.jpg" alt="Gaston, Duke of Orléans" width="320" height="524" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anthony van Dyck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Full_length_portrait_painting_of_Gaston_of_France,_Duke_of_Orl%C3%A9ans_in_1634_by_Anthony_van_Dyck_(Mus%C3%A9e_Cond%C3%A9).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Gaston Jean Baptiste was born at the Palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fontainebleau">Fontainebleau</a> on 24 April 1608, the third son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV of France</a> and his second wife, Marie de' Medici. He was given the title Duke of Anjou at birth and was raised under the royal governess Françoise de Montglat. On 6 August 1626 he married Marie de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a>, Duchess of Montpensier, and received the duchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chartres">Chartres</a> and the county of Blois as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a>.</p><p>She died on 4 June 1627, six days after giving birth to their daughter Anne Marie Louise, later called the Grande Mademoiselle. As eldest surviving brother of Louis XIII he was known at court as Monsieur, and he was heir presumptive from 1611 until the birth of the king's first son in 1638.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Career</h2><p>Gaston held nominal command of the army besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-rochelle">La Rochelle</a> in 1628 and had already begun the political intrigue that would occupy the rest of his life. He twice had to leave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> for conspiring against his brother and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu">Cardinal Richelieu</a>. After an unsuccessful war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a> that led to the Battle of Castelnaudary in 1632, he took refuge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>. Reconciled with the king, he plotted again in 1635 and fled, then submitted.</p><p>He then conspired with the marquis de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-coiffier-de-ruze-marquis-of-cinq-mars">Cinq-Mars</a> against Richelieu and deserted him in 1642. After Louis XIII died in 1643 Gaston became lieutenant-general of the kingdom and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> on the northern frontier, and he was created duc d'Alençon in 1646. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-fronde">Fronde</a>, from 1648 to 1653, he showed no particular loyalty to the crown and passed easily from one side to the other.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Legacy</h2><p>While sheltering from Richelieu in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, Gaston fell in love with Marguerite of Lorraine, sister of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Charles IV</a>, and married her in a secret ceremony at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a> on the night of 2–3 January 1632, without his brother's permission. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parlement-of-paris">Parlement of Paris</a> declared the marriage void in September 1634, and an assembly of the French clergy held in 1635 that a prince du sang could marry only with the king's consent.</p><p>Louis XIII accepted his plea on his deathbed in May 1643, and the couple married a third time that July at Meudon. They had five children, of whom three daughters survived to adulthood. After Louis's death Gaston was called Le Grand Monsieur to tell him from his nephew Philippe. Cardinal Mazarin exiled him to Blois in 1652, and he stayed there until he died on 2 February 1660; his titles passed to his nephew.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Gaston, Duke of Orléans” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Charles IV’s alliance with the Habsburgs and with Louis XIII’s rebellious brother <b>Gaston of Orléans</b>, who secretly married the duke’s sister Marguerite, provoked French invasion in 1633; the duchy was occupied for most of the next three decades and ravaged by war, plague and famine.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-lorraine">Duchy of Lorraine · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Palace of Fontainebleau, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in Château de Blois, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.4,2.7&amp;year=1641" aria-label="Palace of Fontainebleau on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4613 471 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Gaston, Duke of Orléans"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5063 741h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5063 741h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.4,2.7&amp;year=1641">What was here in 1641? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
